frankensim-shell-assembly-options-v1
# MaroonOak (MB 15931; spec8 MB 136): a CELLO body for the material_strings shell route, table cello-h12.5-s8-v5.tsv (39 parts,
# 11213 nodes, 17514 triangles, 92 ties; specimen spec8 = f-holes placed from the LOC Castelbarco caliper sheet): published maker
# values (Johannsson cello table, Hargrave 'Servais' / Sacconi, LOC Castelbarco bouts and f-holes)
# mapped onto the il Cannone specimen tables; every mapped value and every ASSUMPTION is in the specimen's PROVENANCE.tsv. Not a scanned cello.
# Every choice is cannone-h6.assembly's except the projection work and the one bridge: the window is the same 15 Hz-5 kHz
# (the spruce pack's source band ends at 5 kHz), the same two violin shell packs.
window-hz 15 5000
# The v4 maximum, 2^41 terms; the documented count for 11216 nodes, 17521 triangles, 256 modes and one bridge is about 1.6e12.
projection-work 2199023255552
reference-thickness-m 0.003
pack spruce @body
pack maple violin-maple-sycamore-sonderegger2013-shell.fsmatpk
# One string per card (a 1-string card needs a 1-bridge profile). The string meets the bridge at this point (x, y) [m] of the
# table (string-contacts.tsv of the specimen: spacing 47 mm C to A, Johannsson); it drives its bridge node along x.
bridge-component bridge
bridge-direction 1 0 0
# D string
bridge 0.007833 -0.112000
